[validators.between.between]
69:25 call  AbsMax()
    note: AbsMax defines no __init__ or __new__; type.__call__ runs object.__new__ and object.__init__, which give no edge (as h11's Http10Reader); @total_ordering only adds comparison methods
71:25 call  AbsMin()
    note: AbsMin defines no __init__ or __new__; type.__call__ runs object.__new__ and object.__init__, which give no edge (as h11's Http10Reader); @total_ordering only adds comparison methods
74:20 op  min_val > max_val
    -> validators._extremes.AbsMin.__le__
    -> validators._extremes.AbsMax.__ge__
    note: min_val is a client value or AbsMin (the default, line 71; annotated Union[PossibleValueTypes, AbsMin, None]); max_val is a client value or AbsMax (line 69). @total_ordering adds generated comparison methods. AbsMin > x runs AbsMin.__gt__ (functools._gt_from_le), which calls type(self).__le__. x > AbsMax(), with x an int, float, str or datetime, gets NotImplemented from x and runs the reflected AbsMax.__lt__ (functools._lt_from_ge), which calls type(self).__ge__. The functools frames between are library code (the callback rule, B5). The site finder proposes no candidate here: the package defines no __gt__ or __lt__ (validators.md, J6)
75:29 call  ValueError("`min_val` cannot be greater than `max_val`")
    -> <builtin>.ValueError
77:24 call  TypeError("Comparison type mismatch")
    -> <builtin>.TypeError
79:20 op  min_val <= value <= max_val
    -> validators._extremes.AbsMin.__le__
    reject validators._extremes.AbsMax.__ge__: the operands are min_val (a client value or AbsMin) and value (a client value of PossibleValueTypes, never an AbsMax), so the reflected __ge__ is that of a client value
    note: AbsMin defines __le__ itself (_extremes.py:45)
79:29 op  min_val <= value <= max_val
    -> validators._extremes.AbsMax.__ge__
    reject validators._extremes.AbsMin.__le__: the operands are value (a client value of PossibleValueTypes, never an AbsMin) and max_val (a client value or AbsMax)
    note: value <= AbsMax(): the int, float, str or datetime __le__ returns NotImplemented, and Python calls the reflected AbsMax.__ge__ (_extremes.py:24)

